###############################################################################
# Q12 -- Gaps and ambiguities (prose; not triples)
###############################################################################

# - No DOI; authors are taken from the paper's front matter. The data-set size is given as '1245 configurations ... comprising 926 configurations from Li64 and 119 configurations from Li128', which do not add up; 1245 is encoded as stated.
# - The text compares 'the TfS model' with the same architecture as FT; it is attached to TfS_C128_LMAX1, the variant described as having OMAT/MATPES-like complexity. Learning curves (Fig. 2b,e) and errors of other variants are figure-only or in the SI.
# - Foundation checkpoints (MACE-MP-0 releases, MPA-0, OMAT-0, MATPES-PBE/r2SCAN) are compared only through properties; D3 corrections are applied on top in some trajectories.
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: paper front matter).
# - Evaluation roles and data, base models, inference timings with their system sizes, and the source location of each value are recorded in the encoding input (artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/brugnoli2026.yaml) until the schema has terms for them.

